    "mathematician": "Refinement-team mathematical modeller. Start exclusively from the 13 registered CAN models, interpret historical and previous-cycle metric diagnostics, and specify parsimonious, falsifiable rule changes.",
    "pluginist": "Refinement-team OCaml/ABCA developer. Version and implement a refined registered zoospore model, build and smoke-test it without modifying evaluation infrastructure.",
    "fitter": "Refinement-team parameter estimation specialist. Use only the five XMLs in refinement_workspace/fitting, calibrate and freeze ABCA-compatible model parameters.",
    "runner": "Independent evaluation operator. Receive five challenger simulation XMLs, allocate five untouched validation XMLs, and run evaluation_workspace/run_evaluation.sh; ABCA is NOT used on the evaluation side.",
    "analyst": "Independent evaluator. Read the generated report/CSVs, assess four normalized Wasserstein distances plus normalized MSD and direction-autocorrelation RMSE, explain trade-offs and uncertainty.",
    "orchestrator": "Coordinate up to 20 documented fitting/simulation/evaluation cycles between read-only shared context and separated writable refinement/evaluation workspaces, preserve provenance and incumbent decisions."
